WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.560
It’s been 4 months since the 2018 iPad Pro
was released and many of you have been holding

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.080
off on buying one.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.680
Maybe it’s just too expensive and you’re
waiting for it to go on sale, or maybe you’ve

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.090
heard some good things and some bad things
about the new iPad Pro, and you’re waiting

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:17.280
to hear if the iPad experience is actually
improved in the real world compared to an

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.210
old iPad or iPad Pro.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.390
So let’s talk about my personal experience
with some of the best and most controversial

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:29.350
features as well as some of the drawbacks
of the new iPad Pro after 4 months of use.

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:33.000
First off, it feels like no iPad you’ve
ever used before.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.079
Even the 2017 iPad Pro doesn’t come close
in terms of design.

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:40.960
The displays all-new rounded corners make
it feel like a part of the future.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.100
And after spending 4 months with it, I don’t
think I could ever go back to a Touch ID packing

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.100
iPad.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:51.209
Face ID works better than on any iPhone, since
it works in literally any orientation, even

00:00:51.209 --> 00:00:52.379
upside down.

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:56.499
After a while, you sort of forget that Face
ID is even there, since there’s no notch

00:00:56.499 --> 00:00:58.960
at all, so it seems to work like magic.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.739
Some people refuse to buy it because of the
lack of Touch ID, but Face ID works flawlessly,

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:05.369
trust me, you won’t miss it.

00:01:05.369 --> 00:01:11.259
The 4-speaker stereo system sounds incredible,
just like it did on the last iPad Pro. iPads

00:01:11.259 --> 00:01:14.799
with only one set of speakers on the bottom
simply can’t compare.

00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:19.219
Seriously, guys, every aspect of the iPad
Pro’s design has been perfected, from the

00:01:19.219 --> 00:01:23.920
Apple Pencil 2 and the new smart keyboard,
which I’ll talk about in a minute, everything

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.200
is finally perfect.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.200
In my opinion.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.399
For others, not so much.

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:32.259
Let’s get into some of the controversial
changes and what I think about them.

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:34.700
The biggest one is the removal of the headphone
jack.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.249
I personally don’t care at all since I haven’t
even laid my hands on a set of wired earbuds

00:01:39.249 --> 00:01:42.260
in over 2 years, ever since I got my AirPods.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.540
And they’re so great that I can never go
back.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:48.609
Of course, I understand that not everyone
has AirPods, but if you can afford this iPad

00:01:48.609 --> 00:01:53.649
Pro, I’m pretty sure you can afford AirPods
and trust me, you won’t regret your purchase.

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:57.520
For everyone else, Apple sells a super cheap
$9 adapter on their website.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:00.069
It’s a bit inconvenient, but it does the
job.

00:02:00.069 --> 00:02:01.729
Now let’s talk about bendgate.

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:06.200
After 4 months of use, this iPad Pro is still
perfectly flat, and I’m pretty sure that

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.780
most people won’t experience any issues
at all.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:13.030
However, a small percentage probably will,
especially those who aren’t very careful

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.030
with their stuff.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:19.840
I honestly think the issue is just way overexaggerated
thanks to all the bend test videos on youtube.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.260
USB-C is awesome, but it honestly doesn’t
make the iPad Pro any more of a computer than

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.220
the 2017 Pro.

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:30.819
The file manager sucks and you can’t connect
and edit files directly from an external storage

00:02:30.819 --> 00:02:31.819
drive.

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:34.780
The reality of the whole computer dilemma
is that most people are just going to be doing

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:40.540
things like watching movies, using the pencil,
using apps, playing games, and doing business

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:41.660
or school work.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:47.130
And for those people, the limitations of USB-C
on the iPad Pro really won’t matter.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:51.220
My favorite part about USB-C is that you can
use your MacBook charging cable to charge

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.810
it, freeing up a wall plug.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:57.430
A lot of people complained that the new iPad
Pro still doesn’t have an OLED display,

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:01.610
but it’ll drive up the price ever higher
since Apple is currently reliant on Samsung

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:07.280
for OLED displays, and Apple would also have
to ditch the iPad Pro’s ProMotion technology,

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:12.430
which doubles the display’s refresh rate
to 120hz for buttery smooth interactions,

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:17.099
including drastically reducing Apple Pencil
lag, so don’t expect to get OLED until Apple

00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:20.390
can find a way to get ProMotion on an OLED
display.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:24.660
Speaking of the Apple Pencil, its new method
of wireless charging makes the old Apple Pencil

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.409
seem like an unfinished product.

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:31.370
The new Apple Pencil feels solid and perfected,
especially thanks to its new double-tap feature,

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.590
which seriously makes a world of a difference
in terms of productivity.

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:39.430
The new smart keyboard folio is now completely
flat and smooth on both sides so it now looks

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:44.269
incredible compared to the old humpback keyboard,
and it also offers protection for the display

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:45.269
as well.

00:03:45.269 --> 00:03:49.180
There are some downsides like being able to
feel the keys when the folio is folded back

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:53.090
and not being able to prop the display up
in theatre mode, but that doesn’t bother

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:54.090
me personally.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.430
Finally, let’s talk about performance.

00:03:56.430 --> 00:04:01.409
Many of you already know that the 2018 iPad
Pro packs the most powerful mobile chip ever,

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:04.019
but what you don’t know is if it really
matters.

00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:07.579
After using it for 4 months, it’s hard to
tell much of a difference between this and

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:11.849
last year’s iPad Pro, even though it doubled
many benchmark scores.

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:15.579
For many years, iOS software developers have
been creating apps and games that can be run

00:04:15.579 --> 00:04:20.540
on much weaker devices to support more of
the market, and the new iPad Pro’s performance

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.610
truly took everyone by surprise.

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.440
We simply don’t have very many apps and
games that can use even half of the potential

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.700
of the iPad Pro.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.170
And at this rate, we’re gonna be waiting
a year or more until we start seeing a lot

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:36.470
of apps and games that’ll be limited by
the performance of, let’s say, the 2018

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.360
iPad and it’s A10 chip.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.070
If you guys watched our 1-year review of the
regular iPad, you’d know that it’s good

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.500
enough for most people.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.190
If you are one of those people who can take
advantage of the performance, definitely buy

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.990
it over the regular iPad or even the 2017
iPad Pro.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:54.060
And of course, there are a lot of people who
don’t actually need all of that performance.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:58.030
They just want the best that Apple has to
offer and they’re okay dishing out the cash

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.030
for it.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.240
Now if you’re somewhere in the middle.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:05.060
I’d say that after spending 4 months with
the new iPad Pro, just all of the design updates

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:09.810
alone without considering the massive performance
are worth paying some extra cash over the

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:13.570
2017 iPad Pro or any high-end Android tablet.

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:17.410
You’ve gotta think about the future, and
it’s much better to have all of that powerful

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:21.940
hardware right now and wait for the software
side to catch up than not have it when you’ll

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.600
eventually really need it.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:24.670
This has been Vadim with Max Tech.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:26.140
If you enjoyed the review, make sure to click
that like button while you’re heading to

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:27.140
the sub button.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.550
We’ll see you in the next one!

